.Dd October 10, 2026
.Dt SCRIPT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm script
.Nd make a typescript of a terminal session
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl aefq
.Op Fl c Ar command
.Op Ar file Op Ar command ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
starts a shell on a pseudo-terminal and copies everything the terminal
shows, to the screen and to
.Ar file
(default
.Pa typescript ) .
It ends when the shell does.
With
.Fl c
or with words after the file, the command runs instead of an interactive
shell.
The file starts with a line
.Dq Script started on
and the date and ends with
.Dq Script done on ,
the date and the command's exit status.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Append to the file.
.It Fl c Ar command
Run the command through
.Ev SHELL Fl c
and end with it.
.It Fl e
Exit with the command's status.
.It Fl f
Flush the file after each write.
.It Fl q
Leave out the messages on the terminal.
.It Fl V
Print the version.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width SHELL
.It Ev SHELL
The shell to start; the default is
.Pa /bin/sh .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sh 1
